Actually implementing timers attached to objects and monsters are quite 
trivial in NetHack.

All timer handling code exists, you only need to implement the functions 
that should be called at the start and at the end of the timed event.

In this case nothing happens when the timer starts and nothing happens 
when the timer goes off.

So you need to insert the timer type into timeout.h and in timeout_funcs 
in timeout.c.
Start the timer in usemisc() in muse.c.
Transfer the timer from monster to object in make_corpse() in mon.c.
Check for the timer and if found stop it and give the gain level to the 
hero in done_eating() in eat.c.

